# ~/.zshrc.local — machine-specific overrides, NOT synced.
#
# How to apply on a new machine:
#   1. cp ~/dotfiles/zshrc/.zshrc.local.example ~/.zshrc.local
#   2. Uncomment/edit the lines this machine needs.
#   3. `exec zsh` (or open a new terminal).
#
# This file is sourced at the end of ~/.zshrc, so it can override anything
# above. Keep host-specific absolute paths and tool-only-some-machines-have
# entries here; everything generic stays in the synced ~/.zshrc.

# Example machine-specific entries (uncomment what applies):
# export PATH="$HOME/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:$PATH"   # Antigravity (this Mac)
# export PATH="$PATH:/Applications/Obsidian.app/Contents/MacOS"  # Obsidian CLI